+# Dogfile Patch 1 — Contextual tools and picture actions
+
+Patch 1 adds the following capabilities in the places users naturally expect to find them. There is no standalone “Free Utilities” button, tab, or toolbox.
+
+## Tools ribbon
+
+- **QR code:** generate and save a 640 × 640 PNG from text, URLs, or contact details.
+- **Exact-size blank file:** create a zero-filled file in the current folder, up to 1 GiB. Existing files are never overwritten.
+- **CSV / TSV to JSON:** convert delimited text into an array of objects; quoted commas, escaped quotes, and quoted newlines are supported.
+- **Lorem Ipsum:** generate 10–2,000 words of placeholder text and copy it to the clipboard.
+
+## Image context menu and Dogfile Photos
+
+- **Extract image color palette:** right-click an image in the file browser or use the palette action in Dogfile Photos. Extracts up to eight distinct colors with HEX and RGB values, and supports copying or saving the palette.
+- **Folder cover artwork:** right-click an image or use the cover action in Dogfile Photos. Creates a 1200 × 800 PNG and saves it in the image's containing folder (or a chosen folder).
+
+## Blank file context action
+
+- The exact-size blank file generator is also available in the file browser background context menu under **New**.
+
+## Implementation notes
+
+- Reuses Dogfile's existing `qrcode` Rust dependency and file APIs.
+- Adds backend operations `util:qrSvg` and `fs:createSized`.
+- No new third-party dependencies.
+
+## Validation
+
+- JavaScript syntax checks passed for modified renderer modules.
+- CSV parser edge-case tests passed in the original Patch 1 implementation (quoted commas, doubled quotes, and embedded newlines).
+- A full Rust compile/build was not run in this environment because the Rust toolchain (`cargo`) is not installed. Please run the project's normal Windows build/CI before shipping.
