+# Dogfile Patch 2 — Pro utilities
+
+This patch builds on the Patch 1 contextual-features project. The new commands are individual entries in **Tools**; there is no general-purpose utilities button or toolbox.
+
+## Added / surfaced
+
+- **Compress pictures** — backend image conversion to WebP, JPG or PNG with adjustable JPG/WebP quality. Saves a copy beside the source.
+- **Upscale pictures** — high-quality Lanczos resampling to a chosen longest-edge size. This is conventional resampling, not AI super-resolution.
+- **Merge PDF files** — combines selected PDFs in their selection order.
+- **Split PDF pages** — extracts selected page ranges to individual PDF files in a chosen folder.
+- **Create animated GIF** — backend GIF encoding from a selected ordered image sequence, with adjustable frame delay.
+- **Extract audio from video** — uses Dogfile's existing FFmpeg conversion pipeline and saves MP3 copies.
+- **Minify code or data** — safe minification for JSON, CSS, HTML, XML and SVG. JavaScript is intentionally not regex-minified because that can silently break strings, regular expressions and syntax; a proper JS parser/minifier is needed.
+- **Diff checker** — exposes the existing text/document/image comparison engine as a dedicated Tools command.
+
+## Licensing
+
+The new image and GIF processing commands are registered in the backend Pro gate. PDF and local text-processing actions call a backend Pro authorization check before operating. Audio extraction uses the existing Pro-gated `media:export` backend command. The command palette and Tools entries also use Dogfile's standard Pro marks and checks.
+
+## Not included yet
+
+- **Automatic background removal** needs a supported segmentation model and model lifecycle (download, cache, cancellation, offline behavior). A color-key filter would not be a reliable substitute.
+- **Translation** needs a defined local-model or translation-provider flow, including language selection and privacy/network behavior. No external translation service is silently called by this patch.
+
+These are left out rather than presented as completed features. They remain the two outstanding Patch 2 roadmap items.
+
+## Validation
+
+- JavaScript syntax checks passed for the new module and modified command/license modules.
+- Rust compilation was not run in this environment because Cargo is unavailable. Build the backend on the normal Dogfile Windows build environment before release.
