+# Dogfile Patch 2B — Background Removal & Offline Translation
+
+This patch builds on `Dogfile-Patch-2-Pro-Utilities.zip`. It adds the two remaining Patch 2 Pro utility features as separate Tools commands.
+
+## 1. Remove image background
+- Tools → Remove image background…
+- Accepts multiple common image files.
+- Uses the general-purpose ISNet segmentation model through the existing Transformers.js / ONNX Runtime stack.
+- Downloads the model once (about 134 MB), then runs inference locally.
+- Saves a new transparent PNG copy beside each original; originals are not overwritten.
+- Model source: `Ko033/isnet-general-use-onnx`, Apache-2.0. The source model card describes general-use ISNet segmentation.
+
+## 2. Translate text offline
+- Tools → Translate text offline…
+- Supports source and target language selection, text pasted directly or opened from a text file, and copying the result.
+- Uses Meta M2M100 418M via the Transformers.js ONNX model.
+- Downloads the quantized model once (approximately 650 MB), then translates locally. Text is not sent to a translation service.
+- The selector exposes 48 common languages from the model's 100-language coverage.
+- Model source: `Xenova/m2m100_418M` ONNX conversion of Meta's M2M100 418M, MIT model license.
+
+## Pro access
+Both commands use the existing `proUtilities` feature gate and `pro:authorize` check. The new model downloads use the existing AI model manager, including its progress display and on-device storage.
+
+## Files changed
+- `backend/src/ai.rs` — registers the two model bundles with the local AI model manager.
+- `src/renderer/js/ai-worker.js` — adds local background segmentation and translation worker tasks.
+- `src/renderer/js/ai.js` — includes approximate one-time model download sizes in the model prompt.
+- `src/renderer/js/protools.js` — adds the two user-facing workflows.
+- `src/renderer/js/commands.js` — adds separate Tools entries.
+- `src/renderer/js/pro-marks.js` — marks both commands as Dogfile Pro.
+
+## Validation and limitations
+- `node --check` passed for all modified JavaScript files.
+- Full Rust compilation was not run because Cargo is not installed in the patch environment.
+- The actual model downloads and inference must be smoke-tested on a Windows Dogfile build. The ISNet model is a general-purpose segmentation model; results vary with subject/background complexity. Translation quality varies by language pair and is intended as a convenient offline translation, not certified/legal translation.
